antaginfo-separatist-title = You are the Separatist for a free { $nation }!

antaginfo-separatist-objectives = { $nation }'s objectives:

antaginfo-separatist-faq = Frequently Asked Questions:

antaginfo-separatist-q1 = "What even IS a Separatist?"

antaginfo-separatist-a1 = Separatists are semi-antagonists that every department is filled with when the round starts. They do not have the permission to freely go about and kill, but rather defend the soverignity of their department. You may actually recognize them by their historical mode they existed from: Nations!

antaginfo-separatist-q2 = "What am I supposed to do?"

antaginfo-separatist-a2 = Each department (nation) has an objective. It's a freeform objective, so try your best to follow it as you would a freeform abductor objective. From experience, eventually nations conflict and devolve into war. As long as both departments know what and why conflict is starting, that's a green light to attack opposing nations.

antaginfo-separatist-q3 = "Is { $nation } the best nation?"

antaginfo-separatist-a3 = Yes.

